From: Verm <183540171+vermingov@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:27:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(linux): size the chrome view when the window maps at
 its requested size

The chrome follows the window through a size request set in the container's
size-allocate handler. GtkFixed has already allocated the chrome by then, and
the resize that request queues is dropped when the toplevel keeps its size,
as it does on sway and other compositors that map a window at exactly the
size it asked for. The chrome stayed 1x1 and the window drew nothing. Give
the chrome its rectangle in the same handler.
---
 desktop/src/platform/linux.rs | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/desktop/src/platform/linux.rs b/desktop/src/platform/linux.rs
index 6ed55943..74069e34 100644
--- a/desktop/src/platform/linux.rs
+++ b/desktop/src/platform/linux.rs
@@ -204,6 +204,14 @@ fn install_composition(
     let sized_chrome = chrome.clone();
     fixed.connect_size_allocate(move |_, allocation| {
         sized_chrome.set_size_request(allocation.width(), allocation.height());
+        // GtkFixed has already allocated the chrome at its previous request,
+        // and the resize the new request queues from inside this allocation
+        // is dropped when the toplevel keeps its size: a compositor that maps
+        // the window at exactly the size asked for leaves the chrome at 1x1.
+        let current = sized_chrome.allocation();
+        if (current.width(), current.height()) != (allocation.width(), allocation.height()) {
+            sized_chrome.size_allocate(allocation);
+        }
     });
     fixed.show_all();
 
